        "y2": 1691.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.4509545564651489,
      "reading_order": 20,
      "text": "6. No. of electrons in a dispositive ion = $a$\nNo. of electrons in neutral atom = $a + 2$\nAtomic number = No. of protons = $a + 2 = b$\nNo. of neutrons = $a + 2 + 3 = a + 5$\nMass number = $(a + 2) + (a + 5) = 2a + 7$\nHence, the correct option is (b)."
    },
    {
