        "y2": 1949.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.8615638613700867,
      "reading_order": 21,
      "text": "7. $\\mathrm{O}^{-2}$ ion is formed by the gain of two electrons\nby neutral atom and $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$ ion is formed by the\nloss of one electron by neutral atom.\nHence, the correct option is (c)."
